			"title": "Reading the Dashboard",
			"heading": "Command Center at a glance",
			"text": "Select a numbered area to learn how it helps you read the dashboard and make informed decisions. 01 Application BarChoose the site, release/CalcEngine filters, change theme, or sign in. The filter icon shows or hides From Release, To Release, and CalcEngine Filter. Leave To/From blank for automatic release resolution. To: Last Complete Release From: First Available Release after To Enter explicit release numbers when you need a specific comparison. An invalid number makes the Release Pipeline and Release Differences unavailable until corrected. The profile button signs in to KAT DataStore. A successful sign-in refreshes only CalcEngine because no other section depends on that session. An amber dot beside a site name means that site's newest release has not finished publishing to every environment. Type * in the site search to see only those sites — see Sites with a release in flight below. 02 Work Items BarLook up tasks by ID, add or edit saved queries, and view saved query results. Query chips toggle the visibility of saved query results and show total count plus ⊗ Critical, ⚠ High, ‼ Priority 1, ! Priority 2, and ⟳ Old indicators. A red or orange indicator means its configured threshold has been reached or exceeded. 03 Release Pipeline KPISummarizes the current release targeted for PROD deployment. Highlights additional candidates, cleanup actions, and commit counts across repositories. The two chips read from → to: the environment and number of the release being compared, then the one it is compared against. Hover either for who requested it, when it published, and the build it was cut from. Candidates are newer releases after the from release; cleanup actions cancel and/or delete stale releases, and are called out in red. Commit counts cover all repositories needed to build the site that will be included in the release. The circular navigation glyph on a KPI tile jumps to its matching card. 04 CalcEngine Pipeline KPISummarizes the CalcEngines associated with the selected site. Total CalcEngines associated with the site, then one chip per environment reading ENV: count - how many CalcEngines have their newest deployed version sitting there. The chips always add up to the total, and each one opens the card below filtered to that environment. Checkouts list users and checkout counts and call out how many _PROD CalcEngines block QA-to-UAT promotion. The circular navigation glyph on a KPI tile jumps to its matching card. 05 Site Scope KPIOne cell per monitored site, worst first, so \"is anything wrong right now\" is answered without reading a number. Hover any cell for the site, its state, and who is on call for it. Below the strip: the OK / Warn / Fail counts - a tone with nothing in it is left off rather than shown as a zero - then the slowest and the erroring sites of the last hour. Those site names are links: clicking one opens the card below filtered to that site, with the scope reset to All. The circular navigation glyph on a KPI tile jumps to its matching card. 06 Site Metrics KPIHighlights logins, page requests, calculation requests, and errors. The tile and its card are titled after the site you are on - sample.nexgen.ess Metrics in this screenshot - because these are the only numbers on the dashboard that describe the running site rather than its pipelines. Site Metrics currently uses representative mock values while the real metrics source is being completed. The circular navigation glyph on a KPI tile jumps to its matching card. 07 Detail CardsEach area of the command center has its own detail card. Expand a card for evidence, management actions, and deeper analysis. Release Pipeline, Release Differences, CalcEngine Pipeline, Site Scope, {Site} Metrics, and Diagnostics each carry a header badge summarizing the most relevant information; release, commit, CalcEngine, and site counts. Each area can be independently refreshed without affecting non-related areas."
