			"text": "The ↻ button in the card header refreshes this card and its KPI tile, and nothing else. Ctrl+Shift+C does the same from anywhere in the app; on a site with no CalcEngine filter there is no card to refresh, so it does nothing. ConsequenceApprovals and Promotions change the KAT DataStore version available to associated site environments. Ensure the CalcEngine has been tested before actions taken. Notable Features Supports 2 environment (QA/PROD) or 4 environment (DEV/QA/UAT/PROD) CalcEngines showing exactly where the 'latest' CalcEngine is running Use the dropdown to filter CalcEngines by environment or all CalcEngines requiring a production move. Blocked Promotions (full pipelines only) shows every CalcEngine that cannot currently move forward, for either reason: a later environment is running a higher version than the one behind it, so there is nothing valid left to promote until the earlier environment catches up; or the upper file is checked out, which stops TFS's automatic Release Pipeline from promoting it. Displays checkout user (including Promotion blocking during TFS's automatic Release Pipeline) if CalcEngine checked out. Clicking chip checks in CalcEngines (forcibly for other users). Quick filter by CalcEngine name or checkout user name. Check Mine In checks in every CalcEngine you currently hold, in one confirmed action. It appears only while you hold at least one, and counts files rather than rows - a CalcEngine and its upper counterpart are checked out independently. Approve and Promote CalcEngines to the 'next environment' when ready. Both ask for an authority email - the person signing the move off - prefilled with your KAT Management Site email. It cannot be left blank, and it cannot be the person whose file is moving: the Approval Authority may not be whoever uploaded the test CalcEngine, and the Promotion Authority may not be whoever uploaded the live CalcEngine. Hover over environment chips to see their state, who uploaded, approved, or promoted and when each environment state occurred. UAT reports a promotion only when the version arrived by promotion - uploading a test version directly replaces that history, so the chip says uploaded instead. Download CalcEngines or view their version history across environments via action buttons next to each CalcEngine. Jump straight to a CalcEngine on the Conduent Management Site via the Conduent button next to each CalcEngine. Conduent Management Site The Conduent button opens the management site in your default browser, not inside Command Center. It appears in two places, and where you click it decides where you land. Next to a CalcEngine - opens CalcEngine Management with that file already selected: .../default.aspx?startPage=lnkCalcEngineManagement&startCE=Conduent_Nexgen_SAMPLE_BRD_SE. The startCE value is the CalcEngine name without its file extension, and always the base file - never the _PROD_ variant. On the KPI tile - opens the management site's home page, with no CalcEngine selected. This button is present even when the KPI has nothing to show, which is the point: it is how you get to the site when you are not signed in to KAT DataStore yet. Download Preferences When downloading CalcEngines, by default files are downloaded to your Downloads folder. You can set the Always Replace and Auto Open settings as you desire. Always Replace - Automatically replaces existing files without prompting for new file name. Default is false. Auto Open - Automatically opens the CalcEngine after download in Excel. Default is false. Note: Once these settings are set to true, the only way to reset them is to use the pencil in the first row of the Work Items bar opens the settings file in VS Code for direct editing."
